cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or discuss this methodology, please cite it using the metadata
  below — and cite a tag, not the moving main branch (see GOVERNANCE.md
  §Versioning: a tag is the fixed reference point external references
  should attach to).
title: "Humanities-AI Methodology"
abstract: >-
  An AI-agnostic methodology for humanities students and scholars working
  with AI tools toward responsible, publishable outcomes: a stack of eight
  composable working protocols (source intake, interpretive framing,
  composition, author voice, tool fidelity, falsification, provenance,
  read-write authority), each distilled from documented practice — no
  protocol enters without an empirical anchor in at least one documented
  practice sequence.
authors:
